  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: LocTab_Core_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Localization::UnityEngine.Localization.Tables.StringTable
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 1e7dd62f4e4c1b940a41f32f228541fb, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 594917404672
    m_Localized: prova en
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290268491776
    m_Localized: Catherine wishes for a mask to rekindle the fires of her relationship
      with her husband.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290327212032
    m_Localized: "Oh my! Such a curious craft you bring to our modest town.. maybe
      I should try out what you offer. Oh, but I shouldn\u2019t.. No I can\u2019t
      keep going like this, see, my husband.. he is a little aloof one might say.
      I feel like our relationship has somehow faded over the years, no matter what
      I try! I think I... I would need something to rekindle what is seemingly lost..
      Something to make his eyes twinkle like they used to when he looks at me. Something
      to remind him how precious I am to him. I wish for him to rejoice in my presence
      like the day we first met, and.. and the day we came home after our wedding...
      I miss being cherished like that... That is what I wish for\u2026 if something
      like that is possible that is\u2026"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290327212033
    m_Localized: "Mask maker! I was unsure it would work but... oh my it did! Wonderfully!
      I\u2019m ever so blessed and thankful, here\u2019s what I owe you for your
      expert services."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290327212034
    m_Localized: "Uhm\u2026 mask maker? I think your creation is working but I still
      don\u2019t feel like it hits the right spot\u2026 could you fix it please?"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290327212035
    m_Localized: "Mask maker\u2026 Your work didn\u2019t give me what I hoped for
      and I\u2019m unsatisfied but alas I wish you to try again\u2026"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406336
    m_Localized: Alphonse needs an edge over his opponent in the upcoming duel.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406337
    m_Localized: "Hey. You\u2019re the one who makes those magical masks, right?
      I could use your services. Ranulf, that tall fellow guard over there, accused
      me of fooling around with his woman. I didn\u2019t do anything of the sort
      of course but he has challenged me to a duel and I\u2019m troubled; I can\u2019t
      possibly beat that lad, he might be dumb as a rock but have you seen the size
      of his arms? I need something that gives me an edge over him, and I need it
      fast. I\u2019m willing to pay you quite a lot if I can return to you with all
      my teeth."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406338
    m_Localized: "Oh my good lad, you\u2019ve done it! I bested that thug fair and
      square! And here\u2019s your just reward."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406339
    m_Localized: "Mmm\u2026 I tried your mask mister, I feel the magic in there but
      I\u2019m not sold yet. Do something about it please."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406340
    m_Localized: "\u2026 Try again."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406341
    m_Localized: Urian wants a mask to reassure the king he means well.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406342
    m_Localized: "Oh.. Kind sir, you are just the one I need, yes yes\u2026 I\u2019ve
      caught word of your arcane paraphernalia and I myself must simply indulge.
      You see, my esteemed artisan, I find myself distraught once more and in very
      much fear for my position as the king\u2019s advisor. Our ever so benevolent
      sovereign has been disregarding my guidance and he even seems a little nervous
      around me lately! Can you believe that? Preposterous. Irrational I tell you.
      I want you to make me something to get back into his good grace so that I can
      continue ensuring the well being of your citizens as I have gladly done so
      far. I shall, of course, pay you handsomely for your services even though I\u2019m
      sure you understand that it is for the good of all."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406343
    m_Localized: "Marvelous! Simply marvelous my dear artisan, you\u2019ve done great
      for our citizens. Here, I am a man of my word."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406344
    m_Localized: "No no, it doesn\u2019t feel right. You\u2019d better not be trying
      to swindle me, my artisan. Again."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406345
    m_Localized: "Listen my artisan, this \u201Cthing\u201D you gave me doesn\u2019t
      work. Make sure you do it right next time."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406346
    m_Localized: Fairlily wood
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406347
    m_Localized: "Fairlily thickets are always a sight for sore eyes. Their winding
      trunks and gentle sways in the breeze makes one feel like they are standing
      in a grand ballet hall, lulled by the world's symphony. \\n\u201CTruly suitably
      named don\u2019t ye think? I me-self would rather work with something more
      durable. Can get ye very neat details tho\u201D. \\nI remember when I first
      worked with this wood I had to discard my first project right away; my hands
      were too heavy and I ended up giving it back to the earth. My chisel wounded
      too deep and I felt like a brute, unworthy and dull, completely out of tune
      with my ideas."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406348
    m_Localized: Heftknot wood
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406349
    m_Localized: "I have fond memories of this most humble wood, it gave my childhood
      home a warm and welcoming aura. That\u2019s probably why I was so oblivious
      when I heard people say \u201Cdull as the heftknot\u201D until I began my crafts.
      \\nThe forests of heftwood trees stand proud and grand over the mountains of
      the Trenchmaw range, though very common, that is the best place to really appreciate
      the duality of their nature. From the hills, their canopies hug their sides
      with a warm embrace, the jagged rocks jutting out like deadly islands in a
      sea of emeralds. From below, the rays of the sun filter only in slivers, caressing
      the thick bark unable to peel off their tenacious essence."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406350
    m_Localized: Grimgnarl wood
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406351
    m_Localized: "Once a fair dame asked old master Berach for a circlet made out
      of this wood, it was to become a gift for her beloved sister on the day of
      her wedding. Old master seemed dubious and skeptical at first but as we always
      do, he accepted the request. \\nOne can tell much about a person's nature by
      the furniture in their home and various doodads, though I have to admit that
      grimgnarl is always an interesting choice. \\nIt is very knotted and difficult
      to work with but at the same time, can be smoothly detailed as if cutting through
      butter; quite the devious wood I have to admit. It is said to be often used
      by the infamous witches of the Lowlands for their tools as well as decoration
      in the folk\u2019s home to ward off bad luck."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406352
    m_Localized: Mighty
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406353
    m_Localized: "Might can be mistaken for power and strength, but as the common
      Hillian saying goes \u201Ctrue might lies in making the right choice\u201C.
      \\nI find that a strong visage is the easiest to carve, sometimes too easy;
      one can accidentally turn a jovial look into a vicious one with just one wrong
      cut. Nevertheless, it exudes pride, potential and can often instill fear. \\nI
      chuckle to myself sometimes picturing the face old master Berach used to make
      for reference, his big red nose twisting the \u201Cscary\u201D expression into
      a grumpy lovable fellow. But drawing inspiration from that when creating a
      mask, courage and confidence flow like a river through the woods veins giving
      the strength to take action."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406354
    m_Localized: Affable
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406355
    m_Localized: "\u201CThe clever lass knows when to smile\u201D, Donndub\xE0n used
      to stammer out every time he had one to many pints. I thought him to be hateful
      at first, I then realised putting up a smile is mostly for ourselves and its
      meanings can be many. Nevertheless it is invigorating and empowering to be
      amiable in the face of adversity, to challenge hardships with positivity. \\nIt
      is truly incredible how one small gesture can shape the world around us so
      much. Wearing a smile will always make one look more gentle and in turn, soften
      the heart of those who look."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406356
    m_Localized: Cunning
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406357
    m_Localized: "The malicious and the smart walk hand in hand, the first might
      take advantage of the second; the second, in turn, might find a way to dampen
      the first. Many stories have been written about this, many characters on those
      pages impersonate these two aspects to a point that we have been taught to
      only see them as evil and good. \\nSporting a grin should feel like holding
      the key to a lock that loosens chains, rather than wielding a blade. \\nWhen
      I imprint a cunning expression onto one of my masks I am always a little taken
      aback; the smirk, it\u2019s piercing, sharp, almost ready to eat me up. However,
      through life I learned to find comfort in the slyness of this sneer, sometimes
      a little subterfuge is the right answer to a conundrum."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406360
    m_Localized: Confirm
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406361
    m_Localized: Back
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406362
    m_Localized: Confirm
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406364
    m_Localized: Adornments of Prowess
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406365
    m_Localized: "I remember drawing inspiration for these ornaments from Berach\u2019s
      beard, I thought it funny at the time but my mind was in the right place. \\nIt
      may look gaudy at first but this finish attunes to a brave heart in a pinch,
      reveling in the perhaps hidden grandeur of a person\u2019s soul. \\nRunes recognize
      when one longs for more and they dance in sync, allowing the arcane to expedite
      the growth of their inner courage. Plus, it is always amusing to see a reminder
      of my mentor on people\u2019s faces."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406366
    m_Localized: Talismans of Judgement
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406367
    m_Localized: "\u201CRemember my boy, you need to be mindful when adding the final
      touches, if you add too many or put them in the wrong places, the runes won\u2019t
      bind the arcane into your work\u201D, urged sage Ruahd\xE0in every time I grew
      too eager to finish my work. \\nThe key was patience. I remember watching his
      expert hands, enthralled by the wisdom they spoke; it was as if the talismans
      were dancing in the melody of his ancient insight, almost begging to bind their
      power to him. But he had no need for them."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406368
    m_Localized: Drapes of Guile
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406369
    m_Localized: "Sometimes the core of a person is concealed by drapes, flowing
      like waves revealing only pieces of themselves. One may see it as a way to
      conceal intent but most of the time the haze only serves as a way to avoid
      one\u2019s fears. With that said, it is not uncommon for one\u2019s nature
      to be shifty, though magic is all-seeing; it is an impartial force to be wielded,
      judgement is only personal. \\n\u201CThe arcane is fickle, but you need not
      to trick it, listen and follow. You don\u2019t want for it to think you are
      its recipient, you are its shaper.\u201D"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406371
    m_Localized: "The crooked cart squeals with each push you give it going up the
      bright green hillside leading up to Aimendell. The crisp morning breeze is
      starting to feel unpleasant on your forehead and neck, beaded with sweat. \\n\u201CA
      strapping young lad like ye will have no trouble carrying this ol\u2019 thing
      around I reckon\u201D, Donndub\xE0n\u2019s jolly voice plays on repeat in your
      mind as you curse at the skies when yet another stone lodges itself beneath
      one of the wheels, halting its stride once more. \\nHe really didn\u2019t need
      to build this wreck out of heftknot, sure it\u2019s steady but way too heavy.
      \\nDonndub\xE0n was like that. You sigh and push forward. \\nBefore the large
      stone brick walls cast their shade on you, you pick up the faint merry melodies
      of flutes and tambourines accompanied by the scent of caramel mixed with hardy
      roasted beef and frothy ale."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406372
    m_Localized: "The imposing sturdy heftknot gate looks down upon you opening to
      an unpaved road. You swear you can see a mocking grin in its gnarls. \\nYou
      find a good spot in the shade of a beautiful fairlily tree and with an exasperated
      sign, you let go of the handles of your cart. You set your tools on your workbench,
      your materials and lastly a dusty cloth to showcase your creations on your
      stand. \\nMany curious eyes eagerly follow your movements, drawn firstly to
      the novelty of your person in this town but then mostly to the arcane glimmers
      radiating from your works. \\nAt last, you put up a sign that reads \u201CMagical
      hand carved masks, for every need, for everyone\u201D."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 290331406373
    m_Localized: You are a mask maker, an arcane one at that. You expertly craft
      wooden masks with the purpose of helping folks with their problem, whichever
      it may be. After being worn for one day, the magical effect will take hold;
      if the client is satisfied, they will reward you with gold to match your services.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
